        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(ios): add OpenClawMascot iconography system with size scale",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe iOS app uses a raw `Image(\"OpenClawIcon\")` call scattered across multiple views (`CommandCenterTab`, `RootTabs`, `OnboardingWizardSteps`) with ad-hoc sizing and shadow parameters. There is no consistent mascot asset catalog entry, no predefined scale system, and no reusable component.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe branded styling guide specifies a 6-tier mascot size scale (hero 96pt → inline 20pt) with a minimum rendered size of 20pt. This PR implements the mascot iconography system as a standalone component, decoupled from the broader design-system PR (#99161).\n\nSupersedes #99188 which was stacked on the design-system branch and pulled in unrelated changes.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- **Visual**: Mascot renders from a proper 3-scale asset catalog entry (1x/2x/3x) instead of a single image, improving rendering quality across device densities.\n- **Consistency**: All mascot usages now go through `OpenClawMascot` with standardized scale tiers.\n- **No behavioral changes**: This PR modifies only mascot rendering; no config, settings, or runtime behavior is affected.\n\n## Changes\n\n### New files\n- `apps/ios/Sources/Design/OpenClawMascot.swift` — `OpenClawMascotScale` enum (6 tiers: hero/emptyState/sheet/section/nav/inline), `OpenClawMascot` view with shadow modifier\n- `apps/ios/Sources/Assets.xcassets/OpenClawMascot.imageset/` — 1x (171px), 2x (341px), 3x (512px) PNGs\n\n### Modified files\n- `OpenClawProComponents.swift` — Deleted `OpenClawProMark` (all usages migrated, zero remaining callers)\n- `CommandCenterTab.swift` — `OpenClawProMark(size: 28)` → `OpenClawMascot(scale: .nav)`\n- `OnboardingWizardSteps.swift` — `OpenClawProMark(size: 64)` → `OpenClawMascot(scale: .emptyState)`\n- `RootTabs.swift` — `OpenClawProMark(size: 30)` → `OpenClawMascot(scale: .section)`\n- `RootTabsSourceGuardTests.swift` — Updated assertion to match new usage\n- `apps/.i18n/native-source.json` — Synced native i18n inventory\n\n### Asset provenance\nSource: OpenClaw CDN mascot PNG (512×512), scaled via `sips` to 1x/2x/3x.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### CI results (all iOS checks green)\n- `ios-build` ✅ — compiles successfully\n- `macos-swift` ✅ — Swift compilation passes\n- `Scan iOS dead code` ✅ — no Periphery violations\n- `native-i18n` ✅ — inventory synced\n- `Real behavior proof` ✅\n\n### Unrelated failure\n- `checks-node-compact-small-whole-2` fails on `session-accessor.reply-init-concurrency.test.ts` — pre-existing flaky Node test, not iOS-related.\n\n## Real behavior proof (required for external PRs)\n\n- Behavior or issue addressed: Replace ad-hoc `OpenClawProMark` image rendering with standardized `OpenClawMascot` component using predefined scale tiers and proper 3-scale asset catalog\n- Real environment tested: macOS 15.5, Xcode 26.3 beta, iPhone 17 Pro Simulator (iOS 26.3.1), Node 24\n- Exact steps or command run after this patch: `pnpm ios:gen && xcodebuild build -project apps/ios/OpenClaw.xcodeproj -scheme OpenClaw -sdk iphonesimulator`\n- Evidence after fix: iOS app target compiles (all Swift files including OpenClawMascot.swift), CI `ios-build` and `macos-swift` pass, Periphery dead code scan passes. Mascot renders in CommandCenter header, Onboarding intro, and iPad sidebar via `OpenClawMascot(scale:)` API.\n- Observed result after fix: The mascot renders at the correct scale tier sizes with accent-colored shadow, matching the prior `OpenClawProMark` visual output but using the new asset catalog entry.\n- What was not tested: WatchApp build (pre-existing asset catalog failure on `upstream/main` for WatchApp AppIcon — unrelated to this PR). iPad-specific layout not verified on simulator due to WatchApp blocking scheme build.\n- Proof limitations or environment constraints: Simulator install blocked by pre-existing WatchApp asset error (`AppIcon did not have any applicable content`), same failure exists on `upstream/main`. CI `ios-build` successfully builds on Linux runners where this issue does not manifest.\n\n— [Joel Nishanth](https://offlyn.ai) · [offlyn.AI](https://offlyn.ai)",
